      "body": "## Motivation\n\nFLUX.2 on MI355 aborts during the first compiled DiT forward. `residual_gate_add` takes the CUDA Triton fast path because `tensor.is_cuda` is true under HIP. That kernel emits PTX `cvt.rn.bf16.f32` with the CUDA register constraint `=h`. ROCm LLVM treats the constraint as a fatal register-allocation error (`couldn't allocate output register for constraint 'h'`) and kills the diffusion worker before the eager fallback can run. Wan2.2 does not call this kernel, so the same launch script succeeds there.\n\n`main` already skips the path when `torch.version.hip` is set. This change uses the diffusion platform predicate `is_hip()` instead, which is the same check neighboring ROCm kernels use. On NVIDIA, `is_hip()` is false, so the CUDA fast path is unchanged.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `can_use_residual_gate_add_cuda` returns false when `is_hip()` is true, so Flux2 uses eager `residual + update * gate` on ROCm.\n- Added `test/registered/unit/kernels/test_residual_gate_add_hip.py`, registered in CPU CI (`base-a-test-cpu`). One test asserts the CUDA fast path is rejected on HIP. The other asserts `residual_gate_add` matches the eager formula.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nThe HIP fallback is eager `residual + update * gate`. Measured max absolute error against that formula:\n\n| Check | Shape | Dtype | Max abs error |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| GPU, MI355 | [1, 128, 6144] | bf16 | 0.0 |\n| CPU unit test | [2, 8] | fp16 | 0 (`assert_close`) |\n\nFLUX.2-dev text-to-image at 720p, 8 steps, seed 42, completed and wrote a 1280×720 PNG. The previous run died in kernel compilation and produced no image.\n\n## Benchmarking and Profiling\n\nSame command as the crash, after the guard. One MI355 GPU, `--enable-torch-compile`, `--warmup-mode request`, `--dit-layerwise-offload`.\n\n| Segment | Time |\n| --- | --- |\n| Full generate, including torch.compile | 176.36 s |\n| Request, warmup excluded | 5.00 s |\n| Denoising, 8 steps | 4.87 s (0.078 s/step) |\n| VAE decode | 0.0049 s |\n| Peak memory | 108274 MB |\n\nThere is no before-latency. The unguarded PTX path aborts the worker.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n## Review Process\n\n1. Ping Merge Oncalls to start the PR flow. See the [PR Merge Process](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/MAINTAINER.md#pull-request-merge-process).\n2. Get approvals from [CODEOWNERS](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/CODEOWNERS) and other reviewers.\n3. Trigger CI tests with [comments](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#how-to-trigger-ci-tests) or contact authorized users to do so.\n   - `/tag-run-ci-label`, `/rerun-failed-ci`, `/tag-and-rerun-ci`\n4. After green CI and required approvals, ask Merge Oncalls to merge.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #37799546565](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37799546565)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #37799546129](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37799546129)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #37799546826](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37799546826)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
